4. PROVENANCE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Problem Statement 26119 required that the solver "shall not be built upon any
existing open source solver library but shall be built from scratch from
mathematical foundation." It was, and this is verifiable rather than asserted:

  - No third-party source file is vendored in this repository.
  - Every #include of an external header resolves to the C++ standard library,
    to POSIX headers used only by the command line front end (termios, unistd,
    sys/ioctl, sys/stat, dirent), to <omp.h> (OpenMP, supplied by the compiler),
    or to <cuda_runtime.h> (used only in cuda/pdhg_kernels.cu).
  - No quoted #include resolves outside this repository.
  - The only build-time dependency is a C++17 compiler. OpenMP is optional.

To reproduce that audit:

    grep -rhE '^[[:space:]]*#[[:space:]]*include[[:space:]]*<' \
         src include apps tests tools cuda | \
        sed 's/.*include[[:space:]]*<//; s/>.*//' | sort -u

    for h in $(grep -rhE '^[[:space:]]*#[[:space:]]*include[[:space:]]*"' \
                    src include apps tests tools | \
               sed 's/.*include[[:space:]]*"//; s/".*//' | sort -u); do
        [ -f "include/$h" ] || [ -f "apps/$h" ] || echo "OUTSIDE: $h"
    done

The second command prints nothing. Every quoted include resolves either to this
project's own include/igaos tree or to a header in apps/, which is the command
line front end and part of this repository.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL USED FOR VALIDATION ONLY
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The following are used by the benchmark harnesses in bench/ and by the local
console in demo/. None is linked into, compiled into, or distributed with the
solver; each is invoked as a separate program or imported by a separate Python
script, and each is acknowledged here as the guidelines advise.

  HiGHS            reference LP and MILP solver, via SciPy's linprog/milp.
                   MIT Licence. https://highs.dev
  OSQP             reference convex QP solver.
                   Apache Licence 2.0. https://osqp.org
  NumPy, SciPy     instance generation and reference solving.
                   BSD 3-Clause. https://numpy.org, https://scipy.org
  CUDA toolkit     NVRTC and ptxas, used to compile cuda/pdhg_kernels.cu.
                   NVIDIA Software Licence Agreement. Not redistributed.

Benchmark instances are not redistributed with this repository. They are
downloaded by bench/fetch_benchmarks.sh from their publishers and remain the
property of those collections:

  Netlib LP                     https://www.netlib.org/lp/
  MIPLIB                        https://miplib.zib.de/
  Maros and Meszaros convex QP  http://www.doc.ic.ac.uk/~im/

